Read `AGENTS.md` first for canonical architecture, hard rules, and delivery workflow.

Read `CLAUDE.md` second for skill routing and close-out steps.

Use repository skills from `.claude/skills/` for task-specific workflows. If unsure, start with `ask-matt`.

Use `handoff` to produce a compact handoff document when context needs to be transferred to a new session/agent.

Do not bypass hard rules in `AGENTS.md`, especially:
- no browser/client direct calls to the Mac
- seam interface discipline and composition-root wiring
- Zod-parse external/LLM outputs before use
